<%#
  Shown in place of reminder-configuration fields when the organization has turned the relevant
  reminder emails off on its settings page.

  Locals:
    reminder_type - :deadline, :distribution, or :all

  From main's #5668. Migrated to the design system on merge: it arrived as `callout callout-info`
  with an `h5.font-weight-bold`, three classes ADR 0011 left defined nowhere, so it would have
  rendered as unstyled text. `shared/essentials/callout` is the component, and it takes the title
  rather than a heading of its own -- design.md, one h1 per page and no stray heading levels
  inside a form.

  `:info`, not `:warning`. Nothing is wrong: the bank has configured it this way on purpose, and
  amber here would read as a problem to fix on a page the reader cannot fix it from.
%>
<%
  title =
    case reminder_type
    when :distribution then "Day-before distribution reminder emails are turned off"
    when :all then "Reminder emails are turned off for your organization"
    else "Monthly deadline reminder emails are turned off"
    end
%>
<%= render "shared/essentials/callout", tone: :info, title: title, wrapper_class: "mb-4" do %>
  Your organization has turned this off, so these emails will not be sent.
  <% if can_administrate? %>
    <%= link_to "Change this in your organization settings", edit_organization_path,
          class: "link-brand" %>.
  <% else %>
    Contact your organization administrator to change this.
  <% end %>
<% end %>
